# gate-checks.manifest — what gate-selfcheck.sh CLAIMS to check, one row per id.
#
# Born P14, 2026-09-08, because nothing in this estate could answer "how many checks does
# the gate have?" without disagreeing with itself: 39 distinct G- ids in the source, 62 ids
# that push a verdict, 101 section-header lines. That ambiguity IS the problem feynmanSync-09
# hit — it tried to read box coverage off gate OUTPUT and measured an artifact of where the
# headers happen to be printed rather than of which checks ran.
#
# FORMAT — three tab-separated columns:
#   <id>  <parent>  <what it checks>
#
#   parent "-"  = a REACH UNIT. Exactly one `gate_ran "<id>"` call sits at the top of its
#                 block in gate-selfcheck.sh, at column 0, BEFORE any branching, so it fires
#                 whether the check goes green, red or silent.
#   parent <id> = a VERDICT ALIAS: a label the gate speaks under from inside that reach
#                 unit's branches. Declared, never inferred from the string — prefix
#                 inference would let "G-A" answer confidently for "G-AB".
#
# THE CONTRACT THIS FILE BUYS: gate-roll-call-drill.sh holds it in both directions. A
# declared unit with no `gate_ran` shows up NOT-REACHED; an id that speaks with no row here
# shows up UNDECLARED. Add a check, add a row — that is the whole maintenance burden, and
# the drill is what makes forgetting it visible instead of silent.
G-H#drill	-	the sibling-downgrade control is still a control
G-H#roster	-	the other two roster drills actually run
G-H	-	repo hygiene sweep: every repo committed AND pushed
G-S	-	orphan code-island sweep (gitignored code dirs are their own repo)
G-W	-	untracked-keeper sweep (a keeper doc git ignores is NOT backed)
G-Z	-	TODO-rider sweep (a TODO may ride at most ONE handoff)
G-I	-	dead-value sweep (report-only)
G-E	-	secret sweep over tracked files
G-T#43	-	strike-zone runtime box parity: repo + ledger HEAD vs gh
G-T#44	-	n8n-spine crontab matches the vaulted provision file
G-T#45	-	n8n provisioning repo parity
G-T#46	-	flowers box repo parity
G-L	-	HANDOFF-GATE canonical doc: header, changelog, mirrors, copies
G-U	-	learning-harvest challenge (lessons banked this session)
G-W#2	-	toolchain canary
G-V	-	AAR/RCA obligation on completed Batter's Box cards
G-V#owner	-	the attribution helper can still tell its five causes apart
G-V#2	-	Asana single-page collection-read ratchet
G-V#3	-	card-lint stale-summary ratchet
G-X	-	FDA grant canary (macOS subject)
G-X#platform	-	the platform exemption fires only where there is no subject
G-Y	-	relay bootstrap freshness (the cloud curl serves what darwin has)
G-AA	-	session corroboration: used leaves must be resolved
G-AD	-	bb-writers ratchet (every BB-gid writer ratified)
G-AE	-	launchd schedule backing (macOS subject)
G-AF	-	pre-commit hook coverage on every repo
G-AG	-	dotfiles installed AND derived
G-AH	-	a log line is not evidence
G-AH#tripwire	-	does the instrument itself still fire?
G-AI	-	no gate step vanishes with its instrument
G-AI#skipped	-	a skipped check must not be certifiable as a pass
G-AJ	-	a renamed object stops teaching its old name
G-AK	-	every ratification still describes something true
G-AK#drill	-	the ratification census can still go red
G-AL#tag	-	the wrap order preserves the session tag
G-AL	-	the session knew what DONE looks like
G-AL#registry	-	a criteria ledger nobody registered is a ledger nobody reads
G-AL#census	-	registered is not measured
G-AL#census#drill	-	the charter-board census can still go red
G-AL#drill	-	the charter check can still go red
G-V#ship	-	a card whose fix shipped is closed, or consciously left open
G-AO	-	an exit code is never read through a pipe
G-AP	-	every declared verdict has been seen to fire
G-AP#drill	-	the verdict-contract census can still go red
G-AQ	-	an inherited thread survives the handoff
G-AQ#number	-	the predecessor's filename is derived correctly
G-AQ#drill	-	the continuity check can still go red
G-R	-	reference integrity -- every gid/path/sha the outbound handoff cites RESOLVES
G-R#drill	-	the reference check can still go red
G-AT	-	THE MAILBOX LAW: no Jason-work stranded on Claude's board
G-AU	-	shared-$HOME scratch is owner-prefixed, never wildcard-rm'd
G-AS	-	the State Machine has a DOOR, and this session used it
G-AV	-	the roll call can still tell reach from silence (its own drill)
G-AW	-	every drill is named by a runner (drill-census ratchet; a new orphan is red)
G-AW#drill	-	the drill census can still go red

# --- verdict aliases -------------------------------------------------------
G-T#43u	G-T#43	sz-tick box probe answered but unparseable
G-T#43m	G-T#43	sz-tick box has NO checkout (absent deploy, not drift)
G-T#43b	G-T#43	box auto-pull scheduler missing from crontab
G-T#43bu	G-T#43	scheduler probe answered but unparseable
G-T#43c	G-T#43	ledger box diverged or wedged behind gh
G-T#43cu	G-T#43	ledger HEAD line answered but unparseable
G-T#45u	G-T#45	n8n provisioning probe unparseable
G-T#45b	G-T#45	n8n provisioning repo behind
G-T#45bu	G-T#45	n8n provisioning behind-count unparseable
G-T#46u	G-T#46	flowers probe unparseable
G-T#46b	G-T#46	flowers repo behind
G-T#46bu	G-T#46	flowers behind-count unparseable
G-L#35c	G-L	the header version must have a changelog entry
G-L#35c#drill	G-L	control for the header/changelog check
G-L#35d	G-L	a handoff_gate.py copy drifted from the kit
G-L#35e	G-L	the header must not lag a version the document already claims
G-AE#drill	G-AE	the launchd census's own control
G-AL#board	G-AL	the generated DONE board is stale
G-AL#done	G-AL	the charter's paperwork has a finding
G-AQ#verify	G-AQ	a carried thread ships no one-line verify: line
G-AQ#selfcount	G-AQ	a verify: line that searches a glob covering the handoff it is written in
G-AS#door	G-AS	cards that walked past the door in the last 24h

# --- judgment steps ---------------------------------------------------------
# Added v1.2 (opus-feynmanSync-11, 2026-09-08). These are HANDOFF-GATE.md sections a SESSION
# walks by reading prose. They have no `gate_ran` marker and must not grow one -- a script
# cannot answer "is what remains crystal clear?", and a script that pretends to is a guard
# that cannot fire.
#
# WHY THEY ARE HERE AT ALL. Before v1.2 the manifest said `units_declared=51` and stopped,
# which reads as "the gate has 51 checks". The gate DOC declares 53 ids; the 51 reach units
# cover 29 of them. The other 19 were not merely unmeasured, they were UNNAMED -- a session
# that skipped G-D entirely and a session that ran it and found nothing left byte-identical
# evidence. That is feynmanSync-09's G-AK problem one layer out, and the fix is the same one:
# give the absence a word.
#
# Their states are WITNESSED / DECLARED / UNWITNESSED and never `pass`; see gate-rollcall.sh.
# UNWITNESSED is the expected answer for eighteen of them today. That is the measurement, not
# a red, and nothing here may ever fail a wrap over it.
#
# THE THIRD COLUMN IS A TO-DO LIST, and deliberately so: each row names what a witness for
# THAT step would be. The next session to want one pays a row-read instead of re-deriving
# this whole question. A row that gets a witness keeps its `judgment` parent; a row that
# becomes genuinely mechanical moves to parent "-" and grows a `gate_ran` marker, and drill
# check 16 goes red if only one half of that move happens.
G-A	judgment	did we capture WHAT happened? A witness would be: the outbound handoff carries a narrative section, not only a file list
G-B	judgment	did we capture WHY -- the hard-won knowledge (the LUT)? A witness would be: G-U already counts leaves banked this session; wire its count here rather than re-measuring
G-C	judgment	is 'the boss' -- what REMAINS -- crystal clear? A witness would be: the outbound handoff names a next at-bat that someone could mark right or wrong, the same test rail-on already applies to a project
G-D	judgment	did we VERIFY, not just assert? A witness would be: G-AR already re-runs asserted exit codes; a broader one would count claims in the handoff that ship a command against those that do not
G-F	judgment	write the copy-paste prompt for a fresh Opus (REQUIRED final output). WITNESSED when the outbound handoff exists on disk at gate time -- which is precisely what G-F.1 asks for and nothing enforced before v1.2
G-G	judgment	improve the system itself (the part Jason loves). A witness would be: a commit this session touching an instrument rather than only a deliverable -- the gate already knows the session tag and the repo shas
G-J	judgment	mirror remote-only source-of-truth into its repo. A witness would be: G-T#44's vaulted-crontab comparison generalised to any remote SSOT the session touched
G-K	judgment	blast radius -- did your change break something ELSE? A witness would be: the session ran a drill or test in a repo it did NOT edit
G-M	judgment	cushion the next chunk -- leave a hands-dirty plan doc. A witness would be: docs/HANDOFF.md in the touched repo is newer than the session's first commit
G-N	judgment	teacher-out -- did this session FEED the tree of wisdom? A witness would be: a claude-blackbook commit in this session's window; distinct from G-U, which counts the leaves rather than the act
G-O	judgment	[unwitnessable] continuation prompt -- verify it is CURRENT, then PASTE it into the chat (the last act). Un-witnessable from inside the gate by construction: the paste happens in the chat, after the gate. Say so out loud rather than pretending
G-P	judgment	arming a dormant capability -- OFF to ON in a live system. Conditional: most sessions arm nothing, so a witness must first establish the step APPLIED -- an n/a here is a real answer and UNWITNESSED is not
G-Q	judgment	DONE vs DORMANT-INCOMPLETE -- a gated, tested half is not a finished whole. A witness would be: the board's own MET/UNMET/CANNOT-VERIFY row for the session's criterion, once board.py can say CANNOT VERIFY (card 1218276652192070)
G-AB	judgment	a successful WRITE is not a verified write -- read the artifact back. A witness would be: for each file the session wrote outside a repo, evidence it was read back
G-AC	judgment	a repo dirtied by ANOTHER session is not yours to clean. A witness would be: the roster claim board already knows who holds what; G-H reports the dirt without asking whose it is
G-AM	judgment	a customer-facing UI is not done until it has been proven ON A PHONE. Conditional -- most sessions ship no UI; an applies/does-not-apply witness comes first
G-AN	judgment	a Definition of Done contains only what CLAUDE can do. A witness would be: G-AL already reads the charter; a criterion naming Jason's hand is mechanically findable there
G-AR	judgment	a handoff that ASSERTS an exit code must have it RE-RUN. Already half-mechanical inside G-AQ's family; the missing half is the outbound's asserted rcs, not the inbound's
